{
  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.gre.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=5608-E": {
      "title": "Research Fellow in Cyber Security and Privacy",
      "description": "5608-E Research Fellow in Cyber Security and Privacy - Jobs at Greenwich Skip to main content Jobs home Login Register Current vacancies Staff Visa Compliance Working at Greenwich Search jobs Equality, diversity and inclusion Sustainability Frequently asked questions Applying Contact us Terms and conditions Cookies Accessibility Faculties Portal Jobs home Login Register Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Research Fellow in Cyber Security and Privacy Faculty of Engineering & Science Location: Greenwich Campus Salary: £38,784 to £44,746\r\n            plus £4313 London weighting per annum Contract Type: Fixed Term\r\n             - until 30/09/2027 Release Date: Monday 12 October 2026 Closing Date: Monday 26 October 2026 Interview Date: To be confirmed Reference: 5608-E On the 1 August 2026, the University of Greenwich and the University of Kent formed a pioneering new multi-university group called London and South-East (LASE) University Group. Should you join us, you will be employed by LASE but will work as part of the University of Greenwich academic division, contributing to its distinct strengths, community and identity while also being part of a wider group that brings together the scale, resilience and shared ambition of both universities. Through LASE we aim to deliver outstanding education, impactful research, and meaningful regional and global impact. This is an opportunity to join a particularly vibrant research environment. The university’s Centre for Sustainable Cyber Security is recognised by the UK government as one of only nine Academic Centres of Excellence for both Research and Education in Cyber Security: https://www.ncsc.gov.uk/case-study/the-university-of-greenwich This position is part of EU project GANNDALF and relates to studying and addressing the privacy-explainability tradeoff of explainable AI use in modern cyber crime investigations. Through agency-to-agency data sharing mechanisms and the deployment of a decision-support toolbox to identify cyber threats, GANNDALF is delivering a customisable and collaborative crime investigation sandbox for scenarios for sophisticated crime investigation. The role holder will help advance our existing work in optimising explainability strength in cyber crime investigations, taking into account privacy. The role holder will also take on the corresponding pilot implementations and evaluations. The role holder is expected to have a PhD in computer science or equivalent and a strong publication record in privacy-enhancing technologies or explainable AI. See the job specification for more details. The post is until the end of the project (end of September 2027), but there is scope to extend further. For an informal discussion about the post please contact Professor Georgios Loukas on g.loukas@greenwich.ac.uk Should you have any queries please contact the People Directorate Team on peopleoperationsdmin@gre.ac.uk Further details of the fantastic benefits and what we offer can be found here: Our benefits - what we offer | Jobs and careers | University of Greenwich and information on the university’s working principles: Working Principles and Guidelines | Documents | University of Greenwich To apply, please visit the University of Greenwich vacancies page and complete all details, including the supporting statements (please note attached CVs and personal statements will not be seen by the recruitment panel at the application stage): Current Vacancies - Jobs at Greenwich We are looking for people who can help us deliver our mission of transforming lives through inspired teaching and research, through our values. Academic Career Pathways We are committed to building a strong, diverse workforce that reflects the communities we serve. We particularly encourage applications from [protected characteristic(s)], who are currently under-represented within the University of Greenwich at these levels/within these areas. We do this through taking positive action such as encouraging applications from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic, care leavers, disabled and LGBT+ people. As part of our commitment to Equality, Diversity and Inclusion, Time to Change Employer Pledge / Mentally Healthy Universities , we are committed to promoting and supporting the physical and mental health of all our staff, and removing barriers to improve inclusion. We encourage applicants to disclose experience of mental health problems so we can support them fully during our recruitment process and make any necessary reasonable adjustments. Any information disclosed will be kept confidential and separate from the job application form. We are making significant strides to understand and continuously improve our employees’ experience and we are committed to implementing progressive diversity talent management. Email details to a friend Apply Online Further details: Job Description & Person Specification Share: View All Vacancies In this section Current vacancies Staff Visa Compliance Working at Greenwich Search jobs Equality, diversity and inclusion Sustainability Frequently asked questions Applying Find jobs Jobs by email Jobs by RSS Search jobs: Search Advanced job search Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten details Register Contact us | Terms and conditions | Cookies | Accessibility © University of Greenwich"
    },
    "https://jobs.gre.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=5615": {
      "title": "KTP Associate",
      "description": "5615 KTP Associate - Digital Manufacturing & Innovative Product Development - Jobs at Greenwich Skip to main content Jobs home Login Register Current vacancies Staff Visa Compliance Working at Greenwich Search jobs Equality, diversity and inclusion Sustainability Frequently asked questions Applying Contact us Terms and conditions Cookies Accessibility Faculties Portal Jobs home Login Register Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies KTP Associate - Digital Manufacturing & Innovative Product Development School of Engineering Location: Medway Campus Contract Type: Fixed Term\r\n             - for 24 months Release Date: Friday 02 October 2026 Closing Date: Thursday 15 October 2026 Interview Date: Friday 23 October 2026 Reference: 5615 On 1st August 2026, The University of Greenwich and the University of Kent formed a pioneering new multi-university group called London and South- East (LASE) University Group. Should you join us, you will be employed by LASE but will work as part of the University of Greenwich academic division, contributing to its distinct strengths, community and identity while also being part of a wider group that brings together the scale, resilience and shared ambition of both universities. Through LASE we aim to deliver outstanding education, impactful research, and meaningful regional and global impact. About the Partnership The University of Greenwich has secured a Knowledge Transfer Partnership (KTP) grant from Innovate UK to deliver a transformative digital manufacturing project in collaboration with Moorside Precision Limited, a Dorset-based specialist in high-quality precision manufacturing. The project focuses on digital transformation and the integration of emerging technologies into Moorside Precision Limited 's production value chain, through AI-driven product development, digital manufacturing, and sustainable innovation. This partnership addresses a critical challenge facing many UK SMEs: transitioning from traditional, skills-based operations to a digitally enabled enterprise. The project will help Moorside Precision Limited move from traditional manufacturing operations toward becoming a regional leader in digital manufacturing — enabling diversification into overseas exports and high-growth sectors such as aerospace, defence and healthcare, and supporting long-term, sustainable competitiveness. Role Overview and Key Responsibilities As the KTP Associate, you will be responsible for the day-to-day delivery of the project within Moorside Precision Limited, acting as the vital link between the company's shop floor and management, and the University of Greenwich's academic expertise. You will drive innovative design and product development, and the embedding of digital and AI-enabled systems across the company's design, planning, production, and quality functions — building lasting internal capability rather than a one-off solution. You will manage the project largely independently, applying strong problem-solving, project management, team working and communication skills, while drawing on regular supervision and technical support from both your Academic and Company Supervisors. The work plan will be reviewed and adjusted throughout the project to respond to new challenges and industrial needs. Over the course of the project, you will develop into a genuine change agent within the business. While employment is with the University of Greenwich, the role taker will be based and will work in the Moorside Precision Limited’s office in Dorset . Why Join Us? Joint supervision and mentoring from experienced academic staff at the University of Greenwich (Faculty of Engineering and Science) and senior management at Moorside Precision Limited. A unique opportunity to work on a high-impact, Innovate UK-funded digital transformation project within a growing advanced manufacturing SME. Establish yourself as a leading expert in Digital Manufacturing and Innovative Product Development. A structured programme of professional development, including access to KTP-funded training and the opportunity to work toward a recognised management qualification. Significant scope for career progression: many KTP Associates go on to secure permanent leadership roles within their host company, pursue further academic study, or build specialist industry careers. If you have questions about this KTP vacancy, contact Keith Casson on k.casson@gre.ac.uk or Associate Prof. Chi Hieu Le on C.H.Le@gre.ac.uk Should you have any recruitment related queries please contact the People Directorate Team on peopleoperationsdmin@gre.ac.uk Further details of the fantastic benefits and what we offer can be found here: Our benefits - what we offer | Jobs and careers | University of Greenwich and information on the university’s working principles: Working Principles and Guidelines | Documents | University of Greenwich To apply, please visit the University of Greenwich vacancies page and complete all details, including the supporting statements (please note attached CVs and personal statements will not be seen by the recruitment panel at the application stage): Current Vacancies - Jobs at Greenwich We are looking for people who can help us deliver our mission of transforming lives through inspired teaching and research, through our values. Academic Career Pathways We are committed to building a strong, diverse workforce that reflects the communities we serve. We particularly encourage applications from [protected characteristic(s)], who are currently under-represented within the University of Greenwich at these levels/within these areas. We do this through taking positive action such as encouraging applications from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic, care leavers, disabled and LGBT+ people. As part of our commitment to Equality, Diversity and Inclusion, Time to Change Employer Pledge / Mentally Healthy Universities , we are committed to promoting and supporting the physical and mental health of all our staff, and removing barriers to improve inclusion. We encourage applicants to disclose experience of mental health problems so we can support them fully during our recruitment process and make any necessary reasonable adjustments. Any information disclosed will be kept confidential and separate from the job application form. We are making significant strides to understand and continuously improve our employees’ experience and we are committed to implementing progressive diversity talent management. Email details to a friend Apply Online Further details: Job Description & Person Specification Share: View All Vacancies In this section Current vacancies Staff Visa Compliance Working at Greenwich Search jobs Equality, diversity and inclusion Sustainability Frequently asked questions Applying Find jobs Jobs by email Jobs by RSS Search jobs: Search Advanced job search Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten details Register Contact us | Terms and conditions | Cookies | Accessibility © University of Greenwich"
    },
    "https://jobs.gre.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=5613": {
      "title": "5613 Apprenticeships Operations Manager",
      "description": "5613 Apprenticeships Operations Manager - Jobs at Greenwich Skip to main content Jobs home Login Register Current vacancies Staff Visa Compliance Working at Greenwich Search jobs Equality, diversity and inclusion Sustainability Frequently asked questions Applying Contact us Terms and conditions Cookies Accessibility Faculties Portal Jobs home Login Register More ▼ Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept cookies Apprenticeships Operations Manager Apprenticeships Location: Greenwich Campus Salary: £46,049 to £56,535\n            plus £5586 London weighting per annum Contract Type: Fixed Term\n             - July 2028 Release Date: Thursday 01 October 2026 Closing Date: Thursday 15 October 2026 Interview Date: To be confirmed Reference: 5613 On the 1 August 2026, the University of Greenwich and the University of Kent will form a pioneering new multi-university group called London and South-East (LASE) University Group. Should you join us, you will be employed by LASE but will work as part of the University of Greenwich academic division, contributing to its distinct strengths, community and identity while also being part of a wider group that brings together the scale, resilience and shared ambition of both universities. Through LASE we aim to deliver outstanding education, impactful research, and meaningful regional and global impact. Apprenticeships play a key part in the University’s 2030 strategy ‘Education without Boundaries’, and we have ambitious plans to grow our apprenticeship provision across all faculties. This is a senior role within the Directorate of Employability and Apprenticeships, where you will principally lead operations of the apprenticeship team at the University of Greenwich to ensure an effective and compliant apprenticeship provision. This role is part of the Apprenticeship Hub, part of a broader team that is the Directorate of Employability and Apprenticeships. We are looking for an individual who has significant experience in: leading all aspects of compliance and operations for an apprenticeship provision within a higher education institute, demonstrable leadership, team and project management skills, with expert knowledge and understanding of funding regulations and requirements, compliance and quality assurance processes, with experience of leading a Department for Education (formally ESFA) audit, and supporting external quality assurance monitoring inspections from the Office for Students. Excellent communication skills with the ability to be an agile thinker and confident decision-maker are integral to this role. The successful candidate will join us at a pivotal time of our provision’s development as we develop our learner management system (APTEM) capability and transition from the University of Greenwich to the London and South East University Group (LASE). Our apprenticeship delivery takes place at all 3 of our university campuses - Avery Hill, Medway, and Greenwich, and we would expect the successful candidate to show presence at every campus as required. There is a minimum requirement of 2 days a week working onsite, with the pre-dominant campus for this role being Greenwich. For an informal discussion about the post please contact Rachel Brandwood on R.Brandwood@greenwich.ac.uk Should you have any queries please contact the People Directorate Team on peopleoperationsdmin@gre.ac.uk Further details of the fantastic benefits and what we offer can be found here: Our benefits - what we offer | Jobs and careers | University of Greenwich and information on the university’s working principles: Working Principles and Guidelines | Documents | University of Greenwich To apply, please visit the University of Greenwich vacancies page and complete all details, including the supporting statements (please note attached CVs and personal statements will not be seen by the recruitment panel at the application stage): Current Vacancies - Jobs at Greenwich We are looking for people who can help us deliver our mission of transforming lives through inspired teaching and research, through our values. Academic Career Pathways We are committed to building a strong, diverse workforce that reflects the communities we serve. We particularly encourage applications from [protected characteristic(s)], who are currently under-represented within the University of Greenwich at these levels/within these areas. We do this through taking positive action such as encouraging applications from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic, care leavers, disabled and LGBT+ people. As part of our commitment to Equality, Diversity and Inclusion, Time to Change Employer Pledge / Mentally Healthy Universities , we are committed to promoting and supporting the physical and mental health of all our staff, and removing barriers to improve inclusion. We encourage applicants to disclose experience of mental health problems so we can support them fully during our recruitment process and make any necessary reasonable adjustments. Any information disclosed will be kept confidential and separate from the job application form. We are making significant strides to understand and continuously improve our employees’ experience and we are committed to implementing progressive diversity talent management. Email details to a friend Apply online Further details: Job Description & Person Specification Share: View All Vacancies In this section Current vacancies Staff Visa Compliance Working at Greenwich Search jobs Equality, diversity and inclusion Sustainability Frequently asked questions Applying Find jobs Jobs by email Jobs by RSS Search jobs: Search Advanced job search Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten details Register Contact us | Terms and conditions | Cookies | Accessibility © University of Greenwich"
    },
    "https://jobs.gre.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=5543-E2": {
      "title": "5543-E2 Faculty Senior Resources & Procurement Officer",
      "description": "5543-E2 Faculty Senior Resources & Procurement Officer - Jobs at Greenwich Skip to main content Jobs home Login Register Current vacancies Staff Visa Compliance Working at Greenwich Search jobs Equality, diversity and inclusion Sustainability Frequently asked questions Applying Contact us Terms and conditions Cookies Accessibility Faculties Portal Jobs home Login Register More ▼ Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept cookies Faculty Senior Resources & Procurement Officer Greenwich Business School Professional Services Location: Greenwich Campus Salary: £32,080 to £37,694\n            plus £5586 London weighting per annum Contract Type: Permanent Release Date: Monday 28 September 2026 Closing Date: Monday 19 October 2026 Interview Date: To be confirmed Reference: 5543-E2 On 1st August 2026, The University of Greenwich and the University of Kent formed a pioneering new multi-university group called London and South- East (LASE) University Group. Should you join us, you will be employed by LASE but will work as part of the University of Greenwich academic division, contributing to its distinct strengths, community and identity while also being part of a wider group that brings together the scale, resilience and shared ambition of both universities. Through LASE we aim to deliver outstanding education, impactful research, and meaningful regional and global impact. Greenwich Business School is one of four faculties at the University of Greenwich and provides a wide range or postgraduate and undergraduate programmes. The faculty is located on the Greenwich Maritime Campus, a UNESCO world heritage site. The purpose of the role will be to develop and maintain effective and efficient administrative and financial systems within the faculty and provide administrative support to the Business Operations Manager. The focus of the role is to maintain oversight of budgets and monthly reporting activities as well as oversee day-to-day finance administration to include processing purchase orders, invoices, expenses, maintaining the school financial database and general administrative duties to ensure all financial reporting and payments are made within the financial year. The post-holder must be able to work as part of a team to ensure that the wider financial administrative tasks within the Greenwich Business School are achieved. The successful candidate must hold a Degree or professional qualification and/or extensive relevant financial administrative experience. This role combines the need for excellent administrative skills, organisation skills, record keeping, confidentiality, attention to detail, a collaborative approach and the ability to develop good relationships with university stakeholders and staff. This role is not a central procurement role and will involve support and oversight to faculty specific budgets. Applicants who have previously applied for the role need not reapply. For an informal discussion about the post please contact Hester Blackwell ( h.d.blackwellgreen@greenwich.ac.uk ). Should you have any recruitment related queries please contact the People Directorate Operations Team on peopleoperationsadmin@greenwich.ac.uk Further details of the fantastic benefits and what we offer can be found here: Our benefits - what we offer | Jobs and careers | University of Greenwich and information on the university’s working principles: Working Principles and Guidelines | Documents | University of Greenwich To apply, please visit the University of Greenwich vacancies page and complete all details, including the supporting statements (please note attached CVs and personal statements will not be seen by the recruitment panel at the application stage). Current Vacancies - Jobs at Greenwich We are looking for people who can help us deliver our mission of transforming lives through inspired teaching and research, through our values. Academic Career Pathways We are committed to building a strong, diverse workforce that reflects the communities we serve. We particularly encourage applications from protected characteristics who are currently under-represented within the University of Greenwich at these levels/within these areas. We do this through taking positive action such as encouraging applications from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic, disabled and LGBT+ people. As part of our commitment to Equality, Diversity and Inclusion, Time to Change Employer Pledge / Mentally Healthy Universities , we are committed to promoting and supporting the physical and mental health of all our staff, and removing barriers to improve inclusion. We encourage applicants to disclose experience of mental health problems so we can support them fully during our recruitment process and make any necessary reasonable adjustments. Any information disclosed will be kept confidential and separate from the job application form. We are making significant strides to understand and continuously improve our employees’ experience and we are committed to implementing progressive diversity talent management. Email details to a friend Apply online Further details: Job Description & Person Specification Greenwich Business School Brochure Share: View All Vacancies In this section Current vacancies Staff Visa Compliance Working at Greenwich Search jobs Equality, diversity and inclusion Sustainability Frequently asked questions Applying Find jobs Jobs by email Jobs by RSS Search jobs: Search Advanced job search Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten details Register Contact us | Terms and conditions | Cookies | Accessibility © University of Greenwich"
