    "https://jobs.gre.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=5608-E": {
      "title": "Research Fellow in Cyber Security and Privacy",
      "description": "5608-E Research Fellow in Cyber Security and Privacy - Jobs at Greenwich Skip to main content Jobs home Login Register Current vacancies Staff Visa Compliance Working at Greenwich Search jobs Equality, diversity and inclusion Sustainability Frequently asked questions Applying Contact us Terms and conditions Cookies Accessibility Faculties Portal Jobs home Login Register Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Research Fellow in Cyber Security and Privacy Faculty of Engineering & Science Location: Greenwich Campus Salary: £38,784 to £44,746\r\n            plus £4313 London weighting per annum Contract Type: Fixed Term\r\n             - until 30/09/2027 Release Date: Monday 12 October 2026 Closing Date: Monday 26 October 2026 Interview Date: To be confirmed Reference: 5608-E On the 1 August 2026, the University of Greenwich and the University of Kent formed a pioneering new multi-university group called London and South-East (LASE) University Group. Should you join us, you will be employed by LASE but will work as part of the University of Greenwich academic division, contributing to its distinct strengths, community and identity while also being part of a wider group that brings together the scale, resilience and shared ambition of both universities. Through LASE we aim to deliver outstanding education, impactful research, and meaningful regional and global impact. This is an opportunity to join a particularly vibrant research environment. The university’s Centre for Sustainable Cyber Security is recognised by the UK government as one of only nine Academic Centres of Excellence for both Research and Education in Cyber Security: https://www.ncsc.gov.uk/case-study/the-university-of-greenwich This position is part of